# The Go API (api/). Copy to .env and change what you need; every value here is the default.

# Port the API listens on. Railway sets it in production. The Vite dev server proxies /api and /healthz here.
PORT=8080
# SQLite database file; its directory is created if missing. In the Docker image: /data/brandy.db (mount a volume at /data).
DATABASE_PATH=./data/brandy.db
# The built web app (pnpm build in web/) that the API serves, with index.html for any other path.
# In the Docker image: /app/web.
WEB_DIR=./web/dist

# Auth: Better Auth (email + password) in a Node sidecar that the API starts, restarts if it dies, and proxies
# /api/auth/* to. Both use the database above. See web/server/ and api/config.go.
# Signs the session cookie. On Railway it is required (the app refuses to start without it); elsewhere this
# development value is the default. Never use it in production: openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=dev-only-secret-not-for-production-0123456789
# The app's public URL, for Better Auth's origin checks. Default: https://$RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN on Railway,
# http://localhost:$PORT locally (where http://localhost:5173, the Vite dev server, is trusted too).
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=
# The sidecar's port on 127.0.0.1.
AUTH_PORT=8081
# The sidecar's script. Default: web/server/main.ts (the TypeScript source, run with web/'s tsx), looked up from the
# repository root or from api/. In the Docker image: /app/auth/main.mjs (the bundle that pnpm build makes).
# AUTH_SIDECAR=
# Scratch (harness test, never merged).
SCRATCH_REQUIRED=dev
